From d8b15d5803b0738a103a2cbbf9ed14a2d8b02922 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: lucascouts <lucascs@protonmail.com>
Date: Sun, 11 Oct 2026 15:19:58 -0300
Subject: [PATCH] agent_ui: Decline asks first only when an answer would be
 lost

Decline on an AskUserQuestion card threw away whatever the operator had typed
or picked, with no warning. Now it asks first, but only when something would
be lost: an untouched question still declines in one click. Either way a
declined question leaves a "Skipped" line in the conversation, so the reason
the agent went on without an answer stays visible (story 035, R2-R4).

**Confirm only when an answer would be lost.** `ElicitationFormState` keeps
the values the card showed right after construction -- schema defaults and a
required single-select's preselection applied -- and `has_input` compares the
current ones against them on every page, shown or not. Text is compared
trimmed, so whitespace alone is no answer; selections are sets, so a choice
made and undone is no answer either. "Untouched" therefore means "as it was
shown", not "empty".

**Only question cards.** `is_question_shaped(schema)` is true when a property
carries the `_askUserQuestionCustomAnswer` marker -- the rule 0027 already
paginates on -- and reuses `custom_answer_companion_of`; a field merely named
like the adapter's custom box does not count. Every other form, the adapter's
refusal-fallback "Retry with ...?" prompt and MCP connection-scoped forms
included, declines exactly as before.

**The prompt.** `ThreadView::decline_elicitation`, which the card's Decline
button and its keyboard path both reach in the pinned and the inline
placement, opens `window.prompt(PromptLevel::Warning, "Skip this question?",
...)` with "Skip Question" and "Keep Answering" -- the pattern 0037 and 0042
use. Only index 0 declines. Any other answer, Escape or a closed prompt keeps
the question pending with its text, selection and page untouched. One prompt
per card: a second Decline while it is open does nothing. When the prompt is
answered after the question was answered, cancelled or ended with the turn,
nothing is sent (logged at DEBUG), and a queued second question is never
declined in its place. Cancel, Escape in the composer and URL dismissal are
unchanged. One INFO line per outcome carries the session id, the elicitation
id, `confirmation=asked|not_needed` and `outcome=declined|kept`, never a field
value.

**The "Skipped" line.** A declined, question-shaped form now renders, at its
place in the conversation, as one muted row -- "Skipped" and the request's
message cut to one line, no buttons -- in both placements. It is a separate
branch in `render_entry`'s `Elicitation` arm: `should_render_elicitation` and
`renders_elicitation_as_card` are unchanged, so 0027's truth table holds and
the pinned slot moves on to the next queued question.

The adapter is unchanged: `applyAskElicitationResponse` maps `decline` to
`answers: {}` and lets the turn continue, and maps every other non-accept
action to an abort.

Tests: 13 unit tests for `has_input`/`is_question_shaped`, 12 for the
conditional prompt, 7 for the "Skipped" line and 4 that go through the
rendered card's keyboard Decline in both placements.

Pure Zed and generic ACP: it rides `claude-agent-acp-plus` BY CHOICE, like
0043 and 0045, and needs no adapter feature.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
