+//! Decline asks first only when an answer would be lost (story 035, Task 3.2; R2.1-R2.10, Q4).
+//!
+//! Wiring: inside `crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/thread_view.rs`'s `mod tests { .. }`,
+//! declare `mod decline_confirmation_tests;` beside `mod elicitation_decline_harness;`.
+//! Resolves to `crates/agent_ui/src/conversation_view/thread_view/tests/decline_confirmation_tests.rs`.
+//!
+//! Contract (Task 3.2 Objective): `ThreadView::decline_elicitation` on a question-shaped form
+//! declines at once when untouched; when touched it opens a `window.prompt` with the buttons
+//! "Skip Question" (index 0, declines) and "Keep Answering", and declines only on index 0.
+//!
+//! Hostile halves, authored first: the confirmation firing wrongly (untouched card, a choice
+//! undone, a non-question form -- even one whose field NAMES look like a question's -- Cancel)
+//! and the confirmation wrongly skipped (text on a page not shown, a selection alone). Then the
+//! prompt's outcomes: kept leaves everything as it was; confirmed sends Decline; a question that
+//! ended meanwhile gets nothing, and a second queued question is never declined in its place.
+//!
+//! Not asserted: the prompt's title and detail wording (story Out of Scope), R4.1's log line,
+//! and the `Err` (prompt closed) branch -- the test platform can only answer by label.
+
